    <id>tag:my-rss-feed,2026-10-30:daily-digest</id>
    <title>Daily Digest 2026-10-30: Why are good developers so wary of agentic develop; The boundary problem in agentic AI is a platform p; Show HN: Korea-data-MCP – Korean public APIs that </title>
    <updated>2026-10-30T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-10-30.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why are good developers so wary of agentic development?&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/rachels-ramblings/good-devs-wary.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;The boundary problem in agentic AI is a platform problem&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/10/29/the-boundary-problem-in-agentic-ai-is-a-platform-problem/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Korea-data-MCP – Korean public APIs that agents can't misread&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://github.com/YoungsoonLee/korea-data-mcp"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Free CVE feed for agents to lookup vulnerabilities&lt;/b&gt; — Active threat or newly disclosed vulnerability — assess whether it affects your environment. &lt;a href="https://casco.com/cve/agents"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;It’s ok that computers are (sometimes) better than us&lt;/b&gt; — Better visibility into your systems — new tooling or standards that reduce MTTR. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/10/30/it-s-ok-that-computers-are-sometimes-better-than-us/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Building a multiplayer game world with autonomous Fable-class models&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/29/how-i-built-the-most-ai-pilled-company-in-the-world/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bliki: LLM Voice&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/bliki/LLM-Voice.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: DockShift – In-Browser Docker Run, Compose, and K8s Converter&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://dockshift.org/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KubeCon + CloudNativeCon NA 2026: End User TAB recommendations and tips&lt;/b&gt; — New release or open-sourced project — quick scan to see if it belongs in your toolkit. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/10/29/kubecon-cloudnativecon-na-2026-end-user-tab-recommendations-and-tips/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quoting Ben Hylak&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/29/ben-hylak/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
  </entry>
